# Canonical host is the bare domain rarepond.com (since the 2026-10-20 DNS move to Cloudflare).
# www currently serves the site directly (canonical tags point at the apex). If a www -> apex
# redirect is wanted, make it a Cloudflare ZONE Redirect Rule (rarepond.com > Rules > Redirect
# Rules > "Redirect from WWW to root"), NOT a line here: Pages does not reliably apply
# host-scoped sources. Never add an apex -> www line back; with such a rule it would loop.

# Rentals is its own static section - serve its files directly.
/rentals/*    /rentals/index.html    200
# Rare Pond Media is served from media/index.html at /media/ (Cloudflare serves the directory
# index just like rentals/index.html at /rentals/). Real asset files under /media/* keep serving
# static-first, so the page index and the asset library coexist. No custom rule needed here.
# Studio SPA: any other unknown path renders the app (which reads the path and routes).
# (Missing /media/* files are 404'd in functions/_middleware.js -- Pages can't express a 404 in
#  _redirects, and a root 404.html would hijack this catch-all. See the media-404 branch there.)
/*    /index.html    200
